  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Poultry incoming study visit</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands embassy in C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire and RVO have undertaken various activities in the poultry sector over the last few years. In 2018, Dutch poultry companies attended the Sara Agri Conference. The Netherlands has participated in multiple poultry forums. In 2019, the embassy commissioned a comprehensive sector study. This study was executed by the Netherlands-African Business Council (NABC) with the assistance of local authorities. The objective was to improve the understanding of the sector and uncover the potential opportunities for Dutch cooperation with the Ivorian stakeholders in the poultry sector. The final report of this study led to a common consensus on the key findings among the relevant stakeholders, including The Ministry of Animal Husbandry and Fisheries (MIRAH) and the poultry private sector. This visit is the next step and follow-up on the performed study. It will contribute to the further development of the poultry sector in C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire. An incoming study visit will further strengthen the position of the Netherlands and Dutch companies as valuable partners in the Poultry sector and increase opportunities for collaboration.</narrative>
  </description>
